  "title": "Overall DLT Transition — 2025–2026",
  "question": "Which parts of institutional finance have actually moved onto distributed ledgers, at what level of maturity, and which title, money, collateral, accounting, failure and exit functions remain unresolved?",
  "bluf": "The institutional DLT transition is a selective migration of representation, shared execution, authoritative record, money and collateral state into a federation of programmable legal ledgers and adapters. Regulated CSD issuance, bank-deposit ledgers and bounded real-value settlement are real; common cross-network title, routine central-bank-money settlement, liquidity integration, accounting close and failure/exit proof remain uneven. A fixed definition of done supplies fourteen non-negotiable joins and an R0-R6 maturity ladder; its technology qualification crosswalk now maps the Crypto Hub's governed systems to the exact functions, legal seats, external dependencies and proof receipts that each path still requires.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-22T23:59:59-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The controlling phase synthesis remains frozen at 2026-08-31T12:08:12-04:00. Explicit post-cutoff supplements through September 22 preserve that historical calculation while recording current gates and a fixed comparison constitution. This Workbench cross-cut creates no live-vault, Currency Watch, Observatory/app, plotline or implementation change.",
